{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eed649e2dd5c096","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t                                             ResPCC: A Loss-Resilient Neural Point Cloud Codec over Lossy\n2\t                                                                       Networks\n3\t                                                               Xueqin Niu∗                                                Mufan Liu∗                                     Yifan Wang\n4\t                                                       starry-night@sjtu.edu.cn                                  sudo_evan@sjtu.edu.cn                             yifanw9@sjtu.edu.cn\n5\t                                                     Shanghai Jiaotong University                              Shanghai Jiaotong University                     Shanghai Jiaotong University\n6\t                                                            Shanghai, China                                         Shanghai, China                                   Shanghai, China\n7\t\n8\t                                                                     Le Yang                                              Yiling Xu†                                        Jun Sun\n9\t                                                       le.yang@canterbury.ac.nz                                    yl.xu@sjtu.edu.cn                               junsun@sjtu.edu.cn\n10\t                                                        University of Canterbury                              Shanghai Jiaotong University                     Shanghai Jiaotong University\n11\t                                                      Christchurch, New Zealand                                     Shanghai, China                                  Shanghai, China\n12\t\n13\t                                           Abstract                                                                                ACM Reference Format:\n14\t                                           Point cloud compression (PCC) is critical for efficient storage and                     Xueqin Niu, Mufan Liu, Yifan Wang, Le Yang, Yiling Xu, and Jun Sun. 2026.\n15\t                                                                                                                                   ResPCC: A Loss-Resilient Neural Point Cloud Codec over Lossy Networks.\n16\t                                           transmission of 3D data. While recent learning-based PCC meth-\n17\t                                                                                                                                   In Proceedings of the 34th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM\n18\t                                           ods achieve good rate-distortion (R-D) performance, they generally\n19\tarXiv:2608.11845v1 [eess.IV] 12 Aug 2026\n20\t\n21\t\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t                                                                                                                                   ’26), November 10–14, 2026, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. ACM, New York, NY, USA,\n25\t                                           rely on ideal transmission conditions. In practice, packet loss is a                    18 pages. https://doi.org/10.1145/3767308.3835677\n26\t                                           common issue and can severely distort latent features, causing co-\n27\t                                           ordinate drift and geometric degradation. To address this challenge,\n28\t                                           we present ResPCC, the first end-to-end neural point cloud codec\n29\t                                           designed to offer intrinsic resilience against data loss. Our frame-\n30\t                                           work is loss-rate-aware and adapts to diverse packet loss conditions.\n31\t                                           At the encoder, we introduce a Condition-Adaptive Latent Modula-\n32\t                                           tion (CALM) module to adjust latent feature distributions according\n33\t                                           to the perceived loss rate, as well as a Spatial-Channel Interleaving                              GT               Ours (2.200 Bpp)      DPCC (2.293 Bpp)\n34\t                                           (SCI) mechanism that transforms channel-wise data extinction into\n35\t                                           spatially scattered element-wise missing patterns. At the decoder,\n36\t                                           we develop a Mask-Aware Graph-based Latent Restoration (MGLR)\n37\t                                           module, followed by a Dictionary-based Refinement (DBR) stage\n38\t                                           to recover corrupted features and align them with canonical pri-\n39\t                                           ors. Evaluations on ShapeNet and SemanticKITTI under 5% to 30%\n40\t                                                                                                                                       GPCC (2.487 Bpp)     OctAttention (2.330 Bpp) PCGCv2 (2.275 Bpp)\n41\t                                           packet loss rates show that ResPCC consistently delivers superior\n42\t                                           stability and R-D performance over baselines. Our framework main-                       Figure 1: Impact of packet loss on the reconstruction quality\n43\t                                           tains high reconstruction fidelity under lossy conditions, providing                    of existing codecs.\n44\t                                           a reliable solution for 3D data transmission over practical networks.\n45\t                                           Code is available at https://github.com/starrynight314/ResPCC.                          1    INTRODUCTION\n46\t                                                                                                                                   Point clouds have become a fundamental representation for 3D\n47\t                                           CCS Concepts                                                                            perception and communications [16, 40, 48]. However, their sub-\n48\t                                           • Information systems → Multimedia streaming; • Networks                                stantial data volume often requires efficient compression before\n49\t                                           → Error detection and error correction.                                                 storage and transmission. In practical network environments, the\n50\t                                                                                                                                   resulting bitstreams are packetized and transmitted over lossy net-\n51\t                                           Keywords                                                                                works, making them susceptible to packet loss. When packet loss\n52\t                                                                                                                                   occurs, the received data may be incomplete, causing the recon-\n53\t                                           Point cloud compression; Error concealment; Loss resilience\n54\t                                                                                                                                   structed point cloud to exhibit geometric distortion and structural\n55\t                                                                                                                                   degradation. Attaining both compression efficiency and robustness\n56\t                                           ∗ These authors contributed equally to this work.                                       agai