esist loss at the cost of extra bitrate overhead, consuming\nfurther aligns them with canonical priors. We evaluate ResPCC on          the budget that could be allocated to improve source coding qual-\nShapeNet [5] and SemanticKITTI [2] across a wide range of packet          ity. Recent efforts in the field of image and video coding [7, 35]\nloss rates. Compared with existing traditional and learning-based         explored intrinsic resilience within learning-based compression.\nPCC methods, ResPCC delivers stronger resilience to transmission          In 3D point cloud compression, however, such intrinsic resilience\nloss while maintaining a high reconstruction quality and competi-         remains largely unexplored. While some studies [19, 23, 42] have\ntive efficiency. Our main contributions are:                              investigated error concealment for dynamic point clouds, these\n      • We propose ResPCC, the first end-to-end neural point cloud        methods are dependent on temporal context and are inapplicable\n         compression codec with intrinsic resilience to packet loss       to intra-frame compression and often computationally expensive.\n         for intra-frame geometry compression;\n      • We adopt a packet-loss-aware codec design that integrates         3 PRELIMINARIES\n         CALM for loss-rate-adaptive latent generation, SCI for cor-\n         ruption dispersion, and a restoration pipeline with MGLR         3.1 Standard PCC Framework\n         and DBR for recovering corrupted latent representations;         A point cloud is defined as a set of points in the 3D space, denoted\n      • We introduce a training strategy that explicitly simulates        by x = {x𝑖 ∈ R3 }𝑖=1\n                                                                                            𝑁 . In learning-based PCC, the coding process\n\n         both packet-free and packet-loss conditions;                     is typically formulated as a nonlinear transform codin